<title>GREECE: Bank/Greece independence bill to parliament -govt.</title>
<headline>Bank/Greece independence bill to parliament -govt.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's National Economy Minister Yannos Papandoniou said that the draft law on the independence of the central bank will be submitted to parliament on Thursday and will boost the credibility of foreign exchange policy.</p>
<p>&quot;Our move signals the government's confidence in the economy and its prospects,&quot; said Papandoniou. &quot;Independence means a reduction in interest rates, a reduction in the cost of money.&quot;</p>
<p>Lucas Papademos, the current governor, will be the first governor of the independent Bank of Greece. Vice-governors Takis Thomopoulos and Nikos Garganas will retain their posts for six years, Papandoniou said.</p>
</text>
